<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoMultipleAssignment - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gomultipleassignment/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gomultipleassignment/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 224</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_224/</link><pubDate>Mon, 05 May 2025 15:15:46 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_224/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;1 x, _:= f()&#10;2 x,_ = f()&#10;3 x, y := f()&#10;4 x, y = f()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&#10;Variable declaration. 1. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is already declared, so &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; cannot be used; 2. Correct; 3. Correct, when assigning multiple values, at least one variable on the left side of &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; must be undeclared; 4. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 183</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_183/</link><pubDate>Wed, 12 Feb 2025 00:20:07 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_183/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the correct output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; i := 1&#10; s := []string{&amp;#34;A&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;B&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;C&amp;#34;}&#10; i, s[i-1] = 2, &amp;#34;Z&amp;#34;&#10; fmt.Printf(&amp;#34;s: %v \n&amp;#34;, s)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. s: [Z,B,C]&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. s: [A,Z,C]&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;h3 class="heading-element" id="answer-a"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Answer: A&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#answer-a" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/cLui57mACBf" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Go Online Run&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 107</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_107/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 23:42:46 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_107/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the correct output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; i := 1&#10; s := []string{&amp;#34;A&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;B&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;C&amp;#34;}&#10; i, s[i-1] = 2, &amp;#34;Z&amp;#34;&#10; fmt.Printf(&amp;#34;s: %v \n&amp;#34;, s)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. s: [Z,B,C]&#10;B. s: [A,Z,C]&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Parallel assignment: &lt;code&gt;a[i], a[j] = a[j], a[i]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Multiple assignment is divided into two steps, with a specific order:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the index expressions and address expressions on the left side of the equals sign, and then evaluate the expressions on the right side of the equals sign.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Assignment.&#10;Therefore, in this example, &lt;code&gt;s[i-1]&lt;/code&gt; is calculated first. Since the two expressions on the right side of the equals sign are constants, the assignment operation is equivalent to &lt;code&gt;i, s[0] = 2, &amp;quot;Z&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 070</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_070/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:53 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_070/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In the following code, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is declared, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared. Determine whether each statement is correct.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;x, &lt;em&gt;:= f()&#10;x,&lt;/em&gt; = f()&#10;x, y := f()&#10;x, y = f()&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Correct&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Incorrect&#10;Variable declaration. 1. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; is already declared, so &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; cannot be used; 2. Correct; 3. Correct, when assigning multiple values, at least one variable on the left side of &lt;code&gt;:=&lt;/code&gt; must be undeclared; 4. Incorrect, &lt;code&gt;y&lt;/code&gt; is not declared.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>